About 3D Asset Types
.splat
— Gaussian splat point cloud. Rendered by the WebGL2 splat viewer. Best for capturing real-world objects as photo-realistic 3D.
.glb
— Draco-compressed GLTF binary. Draco is a Google compression algorithm for 3D meshes —
gltf-pipeline -i model.gltf -o model.glb -d
to compress.
.ply
— Polygon point cloud format. Used by the Pipe Dream photogrammetry pipeline.
